---
import { SERVICE } from "../config"

// The frames, on the page that describes them.
//
// Every search from the masthead is a real request to a Ktor service running this library, and
// the service can encode what it sent with the same SseEncoder the golden-file tests verify. So
// a reader who has just read about `datastar-patch-elements` can search for something, open this,
// and see the event, not a printed example of one, but the one their own keystrokes produced.
//
// Closed by default, and at the foot of the article: a reader who wants the protocol will look,
// and a reader who wants the prose is not made to scroll past a panel of machinery.
//
// And closed means closed, on the wire too. Asking for the frames with every search made each
// answer 2.4 times larger (measured, 2617 bytes against 6224) on every page, for a panel
// almost nobody has open. So opening this is what turns them on: `toggle` sets the signal the
// service reads, and asks again for the search that is already in the field, so the panel has
// something in it the moment it opens rather than after the next keystroke.
---

<details class="wire" data-on:toggle={`$wire = evt.target.open; $wire && $query && @get('${SERVICE}/search')`}>
  <summary class="wire__summary">What went over the wire</summary>

  <p class="wire__note">
    The frames your last search produced, encoded by the same <code>SseEncoder</code> the
    golden-file tests check. Not a description of them. The frames.
  </p>

  <div id="wire" class="wire__frames">
    <p class="fs-paragraph" data-size="small">
      Nothing yet. Search from the top of the page, and what the server sends will appear here.
    </p>
  </div>
</details>

<style>
  .wire {
    margin-block-start: var(--fs-spacing-10);
    padding-block-start: var(--fs-spacing-4);
    border-block-start: 1px solid var(--fs-color-neutral-border-subtle);
  }
  .wire__summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: var(--font-size-s);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
    color: var(--fs-color-neutral-text-subtle);
  }
  .wire__summary:hover {
    color: var(--fs-color-neutral-text-strong);
  }
  .wire__summary:focus-visible {
    outline: var(--fs-focus-ring);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }
  .wire__note {
    margin: var(--fs-spacing-3) 0;
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs);
    color: var(--fs-color-neutral-text-subtle);
  }
  .wire__frames {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--fs-spacing-2);
  }
  /* The server writes these, so they are styled here rather than where they are built. */
  .wire__frames :global(.wire__frame) {
    margin: 0;
    padding: var(--fs-spacing-3);
    overflow-x: auto;
    background: var(--fs-color-neutral-surface);
    border-radius: var(--fs-spacing-1);
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs);
    line-height: var(--fs-line-height-compact);
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
</style>
